2045
01:18:41,679 --> 01:18:44,880
This diagram shows a block

2046
01:18:43,040 --> 01:18:46,880
representation of how an MRI system

2047
01:18:44,880 --> 01:18:48,960
works. Starting from signal generation

2048
01:18:46,880 --> 01:18:50,719
to image display. At the heart of the

2049
01:18:48,960 --> 01:18:52,719
scanner, you have the patient placed

2050
01:18:50,719 --> 01:18:55,280
inside the bore surrounded by gradient

2051
01:18:52,719 --> 01:18:56,800
coils and the RF or radio frequency

2052
01:18:55,280 --> 01:18:59,440
coil.

2053
01:18:56,800 --> 01:19:01,760
The RF coil serves two purposes. It

2054
01:18:59,440 --> 01:19:03,600
transmits the excitation pulses into the

2055
01:19:01,760 --> 01:19:06,719
body and it also receives the weak

2056
01:19:03,600 --> 01:19:08,640
signals emitted back from the tissue.

2057
01:19:06,719 --> 01:19:11,120
To generate those pulses, a frequency

2058
01:19:08,640 --> 01:19:13,520
synthesizer and an RF amplifier create

2059
01:19:11,120 --> 01:19:15,600
the correct radio frequency signal. That

2060
01:19:13,520 --> 01:19:17,360
signal is then sent through a transmit

2061
01:19:15,600 --> 01:19:19,679
receive switch, which ensures that the

2062
01:19:17,360 --> 01:19:22,000
same RF coil can switch roles between

2063
01:19:19,679 --> 01:19:24,080
sending and receiving.

2064
01:19:22,000 --> 01:19:26,640
Once the RF coil receives the returning

2065
01:19:24,080 --> 01:19:28,560
signal, it is very weak. So the signal

2066
01:19:26,640 --> 01:19:30,640
first goes through a pre-amplifier to

2067
01:19:28,560 --> 01:19:32,560
boost it. Then it passes through a

2068
01:19:30,640 --> 01:19:35,280
receiver blanking unit to protect the

2069
01:19:32,560 --> 01:19:37,440
electronics during transmission.

2070
01:19:35,280 --> 01:19:39,760
After that the signal is routed to an RF

2071
01:19:37,440 --> 01:19:41,920
amplifier and a de modulator followed by

2072
01:19:39,760 --> 01:19:43,679
a quadriure mixer which separates the

2073
01:19:41,920 --> 01:19:46,080
signal into its real and imaginary

2074
01:19:43,679 --> 01:19:49,360
components. These components represent

2075
01:19:46,080 --> 01:19:51,760
the complex valued MRI signal. The

2076
01:19:49,360 --> 01:19:54,640
analog signal is then converted into a

2077
01:19:51,760 --> 01:19:57,199
digital form by an analog to digital or

2078
01:19:54,640 --> 01:20:00,080
AD converter. From there the digital

2079
01:19:57,199 --> 01:20:03,280
data is stored temporarily in RAM memory

2080
01:20:00,080 --> 01:20:05,120
and controlled by the host computer.

2081
01:20:03,280 --> 01:20:07,280
The computer performs the essential

2082
01:20:05,120 --> 01:20:11,199
reconstruction step, the two-dimensional

2083
01:20:07,280 --> 01:20:14,000
inverse fur transform or 2D IFFT. This

2084
01:20:11,199 --> 01:20:16,800
is what converts raw KSpace data into an

2085
01:20:14,000 --> 01:20:18,640
actual image that can be displayed.

2086
01:20:16,800 --> 01:20:20,640
On the control side of the system, there

2087
01:20:18,640 --> 01:20:23,199
are waveform generator timing boards and

2088
01:20:20,640 --> 01:20:25,679
gradient amplifiers. These control the

2089
01:20:23,199 --> 01:20:27,600
gradient coils inside the scanner which

2090
01:20:25,679 --> 01:20:31,120
are responsible for slice selection,

2091
01:20:27,600 --> 01:20:32,800
phase encoding, and frequency encoding.

2092
01:20:31,120 --> 01:20:34,560
The pulse programmer and software

2093
01:20:32,800 --> 01:20:36,640
interface also controlled by the

2094
01:20:34,560 --> 01:20:38,560
computer dictate exactly when and how

2095
01:20:36,640 --> 01:20:40,880
these gradients and RF pulses are

2096
01:20:38,560 --> 01:20:42,960
applied. Together this timing sequence

2097
01:20:40,880 --> 01:20:45,440
ensures precise spatial encoding of the

2098
01:20:42,960 --> 01:20:48,000
MRI signal, allowing us to reconstruct

2099
01:20:45,440 --> 01:20:50,480
highresolution images.

2100
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:52,719
So overall this diagram gives us a

2101
01:20:50,480 --> 01:20:54,960
complete picture from the RF system and

2102
01:20:52,719 --> 01:20:57,280
gradient amplifiers to signal detection,

2103
01:20:54,960 --> 01:20:59,440
digitization, forier reconstruction and

2104
01:20:57,280 --> 01:21:01,280
finally the image display. It ties

2105
01:20:59,440 --> 01:21:05,800
together all the engineering components

2106
01:21:01,280 --> 01:21:05,800
that make MRI imaging possible.

