01:26:06,320 --> 01:26:10,400
excellent soft tissue contrast and

2245
01:26:08,000 --> 01:26:12,159
anatomical detail, PET simultaneously

2246
01:26:10,400 --> 01:26:14,320
provides functional and metabolic

2247
01:26:12,159 --> 01:26:16,719
information. The result is a powerful

2248
01:26:14,320 --> 01:26:20,560
hybrid modality that combines structural

2249
01:26:16,719 --> 01:26:22,880
and functional imaging in a single scan.

2250
01:26:20,560 --> 01:26:24,880
This PET MRI approach is especially

2251
01:26:22,880 --> 01:26:26,639
important in neurology, oncology, and

2252
01:26:24,880 --> 01:26:28,639
cardiology where you want to see not

2253
01:26:26,639 --> 01:26:30,400
just anatomy, but also how tissues are

2254
01:26:28,639 --> 01:26:33,400
functioning or metabolizing in real

2255
01:26:30,400 --> 01:26:33,400
time.

2256
01:26:34,560 --> 01:26:38,159
This photo shows a pre-clinical MRI

2257
01:26:36,639 --> 01:26:41,120
scanner, specifically the Brooker

2258
