01:27:06,239 --> 01:27:10,880
The scanner looks similar in shape to a

2272
01:27:08,400 --> 01:27:13,120
clinical MRI with a large cylindrical

2273
01:27:10,880 --> 01:27:15,120
magnet and a bore in the center, but the

2274
01:27:13,120 --> 01:27:17,840
bore is much smaller since it is

2275
01:27:15,120 --> 01:27:19,920
designed for animal studies.

2276
01:27:17,840 --> 01:27:22,639
The extremely high magnetic field

2277
01:27:19,920 --> 01:27:24,800
strength of 9.4 4 Tesla gives very high

2278
01:27:22,639 --> 01:27:26,960
resolution and sensitivity, allowing

2279
01:27:24,800 --> 01:27:28,960
researchers to visualize fine structural

2280
01:27:26,960 --> 01:27:30,800
details that would not be possible at

2281
01:27:28,960 --> 01:27:32,320
lower field strengths. With this

2282
01:27:30,800 --> 01:27:33,920
scanner, scientists can measure

2283
01:27:32,320 --> 01:27:36,239
anatomical structures, functional

2284
01:27:33,920 --> 01:27:38,480
activity, and even molecular processes,

2285
01:27:36,239 --> 01:27:40,880
all non-invasively.

2286
01:27:38,480 --> 01:27:42,800
Preclinical MRI scanners like this one

2287
01:27:40,880 --> 01:27:44,639
play a vital role in translational

2288
01:27:42,800 --> 01:27:46,400
medicine, serving as a bridge between

2289
01:27:44,639 --> 01:27:48,400
laboratory discoveries and clinical

2290
01:27:46,400 --> 01:27:50,560
applications.

2291
01:27:48,400 --> 01:27:52,320
By studying animal models of diseases

2292
01:27:50,560 --> 01:27:54,719
such as cancer, stroke or

2293
01:27:52,320 --> 01:27:57,040
