2294
01:27:54,719 --> 01:27:59,040
can optimize imaging protocols, test new

2295
01:27:57,040 --> 01:28:01,040
therapies, and gather critical data

2296
01:27:59,040 --> 01:28:04,040
before applying these methods in human

2297
01:28:01,040 --> 01:28:04,040
patients.

2298
01:28:05,600 --> 01:28:10,480
His photo shows a modern CTMRI guided

2299
01:28:08,239 --> 01:28:13,120
radiation therapy system. In radiation

2300
01:28:10,480 --> 01:28:15,040
oncology, precise targeting of tumors is

2301
01:28:13,120 --> 01:28:17,280
critical because you want to deliver a

2302
01:28:15,040 --> 01:28:19,199
very high radiation dose to cancer cells

2303
01:28:17,280 --> 01:28:21,679
while sparing as much of the surrounding

2304
01:28:19,199 --> 01:28:23,520
healthy tissue as possible.

2305
01:28:21,679 --> 01:28:25,679
Traditionally, CT has been used for

2306
01:28:23,520 --> 01:28:27,920
radiation planning because CT provides

2307
01:28:25,679 --> 01:28:29,920
good information on patient anatomy and

2308
01:28:27,920 --> 01:28:33,360
electron density which are needed to

2309
01:28:29,920 --> 01:28:35,920
calculate radiation dose. However, CT

2310
01:28:33,360 --> 01:28:38,320
has limited soft tissue contrast, which

2311
01:28:35,920 --> 01:28:40,800
means tumors in organs like the brain,

2312
01:28:38,320 --> 01:28:42,880
liver, or pelvis may be difficult to

2313
01:28:40,800 --> 01:28:45,760
outline clearly.

2314
01:28:42,880 --> 01:28:47,920
By combining MRI with CT in radiation

2315
01:28:45,760 --> 01:28:51,040
therapy, doctors can take advantage of

2316
01:28:47,920 --> 01:28:53,199
the strengths of both modalities.

2317
01:28:51,040 --> 01:28:55,040
MRI provides excellent soft tissue

2318
01:28:53,199 --> 01:28:57,120
contrast, allowing the tumor to be

2319
01:28:55,040 --> 01:28:58,560
visualized more clearly, while CT

2320
01:28:57,120 --> 01:29:00,239
provides the necessary density

2321
01:28:58,560 --> 01:29:02,480
information for radiation dose

2322
01:29:00,239 --> 01:29:05,440
calculation. This hybrid approach makes

2323
01:29:02,480 --> 01:29:07,280
the targeting more accurate and safer.

2324
01:29:05,440 --> 01:29:09,040
In this photo, you see the treatment

2325
01:29:07,280 --> 01:29:11,120
couch where the patient lies with

2326
01:29:09,040 --> 01:29:13,040
immobilization devices to keep the

2327
01:29:11,120 --> 01:29:15,199
patient still.

2328
01:29:13,040 --> 01:29:17,679
The large circular gantry houses the

2329
01:29:15,199 --> 01:29:19,600
imaging and radiation components. During

2330
01:29:17,679 --> 01:29:21,760
treatment, the system acquires imaging

2331
01:29:19,600 --> 01:29:23,760
data to confirm the tumor's position and

2332
01:29:21,760 --> 01:29:25,840
then the linear accelerator delivers a

2333
01:29:23,760 --> 01:29:27,600
precisely shaped beam of radiation to

2334
01:29:25,840 --> 01:29:29,840
the tumor.

2335
01:29:27,600 --> 01:29:32,480
This technology represents a powerful

2336
01:29:29,840 --> 01:29:35,280
integration of imaging and therapy using

2337
01:29:32,480 --> 01:29:37,360
CT and MRI together to guide radiation

2338
01:29:35,280 --> 01:29:39,600
treatment in real time which improves

2339
01:29:37,360 --> 01:29:42,840
tumor control and reduces side effects

2340
01:29:39,600 --> 01:29:42,840
for patients.

